      "lesson": {
        "title": "Area & perimeter",
        "instruction": "Change the side lengths. Watch area and perimeter respond.",
        "explanation": "Side lengths describe a rectangle in metres and range from 0.1 to 100. Area is width times height in square metres; perimeter is twice their sum in metres. The drawing preserves the side-length proportion while adapting its scale to fit.\nArea of rectangle A is 6m * 4m = 24m². Area of rectangle B is 8m * 2m = 16m². Both rectangles start with the same perimeter, which is 2*(6m + 4m) = 20m. Changing dimensions affects area and perimeter proportionally."
      },
